  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HoCotec+ Sustainable pig production on a high state-of-the-art farm</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia used to be a net exporter of pork until 2007, when political reasons led to an abrupt closure of its main (almost captive) market: Venezuela. Local pig farmers had become too accommodated, resulting in technologic stagnation and reduction of competitiveness. Other international markets therefore were no alternative to Venezuela, and the sector suffered a strong decline. Today domestic production does not even cover the local demand and Colombia became a net importer of pork.Wilschip Holding B.V. from Bladel, the Netherlands and Porcicola Santa Cruz S.A. from Bogot&#xe1;, Colombia, now intend to form a joint venture, to establish a state-of-the-art, 200 sows, pig farm in the outskirts of Bogot&#xe1;. It will be the first sustainable, &apos;green&apos; pig farm, and they will implement advanced technology, meeting all the latest guidelines regarding animal and human welfare, farm hygiene, food safety and environmental protection.In addition, a training centre will be established for in depth knowledge transfer to members of the National Association of Colombian Pig Producers, and students from the two National Universities. This will be completely new for Colombia, and should result in a significant improvement of productivity and animal welfare for the whole sector.</narrative>
  </description>
